    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, sporting a commanding 81.87 score. His matchup against Seth Lugo is bolstered by an elite park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for runs and power despite a minor deduction for the pitcher's elite hold efficiency against the run game. Joining him at the top of the hierarchy is **Kyle Tucker**, whose 75.35 score reflects his high floor against Bratt. While **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.23) also present strong value, their high scores are heavily driven by the projected weakness of their respective opposing starters, allowing us to capitalize on volume and efficiency in the middle of the order.\n\nTactical situational factors are heavily influencing our outfield configuration. **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill** earn starts not only for their solid base projections but due to specific conditions: both benefit from favorable \"Slow SP Delivery\" metrics, which we are aggressively weaponizing to hunt stolen bases against their matchups. Conversely, we\u2019ve opted to keep **Brayan Rocchio** and **Miguel Vargas** on the bench. **Brayan Rocchio** (56.28) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly missing the cut because his efficiency against Phillips was dampened by a negative park factor. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** remains a high-upside asset with an elite xwOBA of .403, but he sits today purely because he lacks the multi-category ceiling against Ginn that our current starters offer. \n\nWe are closely monitoring the environment for the OF corps, particularly the wind-assisted boost for **Josh Lowe** (+5% for \"Wind Out\"). While **Drake Baldwin** faces a tougher matchup against May\u2014further complicated by a \"Wind In\" warning (-5%)\u2014he remains in the lineup due to his lead-off spot and the scarcity of high-efficiency production at the catcher position. We are keeping a close 